Capstone Engine

Two Capstone implementations are linked into this product, isolated by symbol
prefix so each keeps its own ABI:

* 5.0.1 — embedded in the frida-gum static library (see the Frida entry above).
  frida-gum's arm64 relocator hard-references cs_arch_register_arm64, so this
  copy cannot be stripped. All other consumers keep using it.
* 6.0 — sources under x/capstone6/, compiled for AArch64 only by
  scripts/build-capstone6.sh into libcapstone6.a. Its defined global symbols
  Symbols that collide with frida-gum's 5.0.1 copy (public APIs and internal
  helpers such as id2name / map_cs_id) are renamed with a `flx6` prefix by a
  two-pass compile using -D macros over the intersection of both symbol sets.
  Undefined libc symbols stay untouched. x/Disassembler/UCDisassembler.m consumes this
  copy through the prefixed API. Capstone 6 decodes SME2, SVE2p1, MTE4 and
  Apple AMX instructions found on A19 Pro; 5.0.1's decoder table predates all
  of those extensions.

Both are Capstone, https://github.com/capstone-engine/capstone

